<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"/><title>2013 Death Files | Matrix Reprogrammed</title><meta name="description" content="High-profile deaths and living evidence dossiers for 2013."/><meta property="og:title" content="2013 Death Files | Matrix Reprogrammed"/><meta property="og:description" content="High-profile deaths and living evidence dossiers for 2013."/><link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css"/><link rel="stylesheet" href="fixes.css"/><link rel="stylesheet" href="cinematic-pathways.css"/></head><body><canvas id="matrix"></canvas><div class="signal-face"></div><div class="veil"></div><div class="page"><header class="wrap topbar"><a class="brand" href="index.html"><img src="sigil.png" alt="Matrix Reprogrammed sigil" decoding="async" /> MATRIX REPROGRAMMED</a><nav class="nav"><a href="index.html">Home</a><a href="death-files.html">Death Files</a><a href="investigation-machine.html">Investigations</a><a href="epstein-files.html">Epstein</a><a href="tracker-dashboard.html">Trackers</a><a href="source-document-vault.html">Sources</a><a href="forum.html">Signal Boards</a><a href="search.html">Search</a><a href="contact-the-machine.html">Contact</a></nav></header><main><section class="hero wrap death-year-hero"><div class="eyebrow">The Death Files · Year Archive</div><h1>2013</h1><p class="lead">The people, official accounts, evidence trails, consequences, and unanswered questions that remain attached to this year.</p><div class="cta-row"><a class="btn" href="death-files.html#year-archive">All Years</a><a class="btn alt" href="death-files-pattern-lab.html">Pattern Lab</a></div></section><section class="section wrap"><h2>Dossiers</h2><div class="grid"><article class="card death-card" data-death-card="aaron-swartz"><span class="label">2013 · Technologist · Suicide</span><h3>Aaron Swartz</h3><p>Swartz campaigned for open knowledge, internet freedom, and limits on surveillance and faced aggressive federal prosecution over JSTOR downloads. His death led to major reform campaigns around computer-crime law, open access, and prosecutorial power.</p><p><span class="pill death-grade">Baseline dossier published; continuing evidence review</span></p><div class="death-facts"><span>11 Jan 2013</span><span>Brooklyn, New York, United States</span><span>Suicide</span></div><div class="cta-row small"><a class="btn" href="death-file-aaron-swartz.html">Open dossier</a><a class="btn alt" href="death-file-aaron-swartz.html#signal-drop">Signal Drop</a></div></article><article class="card death-card" data-death-card="hugo-chavez"><span class="label">2013 · Political leader · Natural death</span><h3>Hugo Chávez</h3><p>Chávez led resource nationalism, regional integration, oil diplomacy, and resistance to U.S.-aligned economic policy. His death triggered succession under Nicolás Maduro and a new phase of Venezuelan crisis.</p><p><span class="pill death-grade">Baseline dossier published; continuing evidence review</span></p><div class="death-facts"><span>5 Mar 2013</span><span>Caracas, Venezuela</span><span>Natural death</span></div><div class="cta-row small"><a class="btn" href="death-file-hugo-chavez.html">Open dossier</a><a class="btn alt" href="death-file-hugo-chavez.html#signal-drop">Signal Drop</a></div></article><article class="card death-card" data-death-card="boris-berezovsky"><span class="label">2013 · Oligarch · Open verdict</span><h3>Boris Berezovsky</h3><p>Berezovsky had helped shape post-Soviet power, later broke with Vladimir Putin, financed opposition, and held sensitive knowledge of oligarch and intelligence networks. His death closed a major source of allegations about Kremlin-era oligarchic power.</p><p><span class="pill death-grade">Baseline dossier published; continuing evidence review</span></p><div class="death-facts"><span>23 Mar 2013</span><span>Berkshire, United Kingdom</span><span>Open conclusion at inquest</span></div><div class="cta-row small"><a class="btn" href="death-file-boris-berezovsky.html">Open dossier</a><a class="btn alt" href="death-file-boris-berezovsky.html#signal-drop">Signal Drop</a></div></article><article class="card death-card" data-death-card="michael-hastings"><span class="label">2013 · Journalist · Road death</span><h3>Michael Hastings</h3><p>Hastings had exposed senior military leadership, criticised surveillance, and was reportedly pursuing another sensitive story. His death became a central case in fears about connected-car vulnerabilities and journalist surveillance.</p><p><span class="pill death-grade">Baseline dossier published; continuing evidence review</span></p><div class="death-facts"><span>18 Jun 2013</span><span>Los Angeles, California, United States</span><span>Accident</span></div><div class="cta-row small"><a class="btn" href="death-file-michael-hastings.html">Open dossier</a><a class="btn alt" href="death-file-michael-hastings.html#signal-drop">Signal Drop</a></div></article></div></section><section class="section wrap"><h2>Year Pattern Boundary</h2><article class="card"><p>Shared dates, institutions, investigators, lawyers, beneficiaries, or security failures are leads for comparison. A pattern does not establish coordination.</p></article></section><!-- cinematic-pathways:start --><section class="matrix-pathways" aria-labelledby="matrix-pathways-title-death-files-year-2013"><div class="matrix-pathways-head"><div><span class="matrix-pathways-eyebrow">Trace the final consequence</span><h2 id="matrix-pathways-title-death-files-year-2013">Connect the death, the context, the network and the missing record.</h2><p>A death file should never stand alone. Follow the person, the institutions around them, the evidence boundary and unresolved questions.</p></div><a class="matrix-pathways-map-link" href="investigation-pathways.html">Open full signal map</a></div><div class="matrix-pathways-sequence" aria-label="Investigation sequence"><span>Discover</span><i></i><span>Investigate</span><i></i><span>Verify</span><i></i><span>Act</span></div><div class="matrix-pathway-grid"><a class="matrix-pathway-card" href="death-files.html"><span class="matrix-pathway-number">01</span><span class="matrix-pathway-card-copy"><strong>Return to the archive</strong><small>Browse the Death Files by year, person and unresolved evidence lane.</small></span><span class="matrix-pathway-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="matrix-pathway-card" href="evidence-vault.html"><span class="matrix-pathway-number">02</span><span class="matrix-pathway-card-copy"><strong>Check the record</strong><small>Open court, medical, official and archival source routes where available.</small></span><span class="matrix-pathway-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="matrix-pathway-card" href="network-maps.html"><span class="matrix-pathway-number">03</span><span class="matrix-pathway-card-copy"><strong>Map the connections</strong><small>See how the person connects to institutions, money, operations and other dossiers.</small></span><span class="matrix-pathway-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="matrix-pathway-card" href="forum.html"><span class="matrix-pathway-number">04</span><span class="matrix-pathway-card-copy"><strong>Submit evidence</strong><small>Add a documented lead or missing record for review.</small></span><span class="matrix-pathway-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><p class="matrix-pathways-boundary"><strong>Death Files:</strong> Follow the records, preserve uncertainty and treat association as context rather than proof.</p></section><!-- cinematic-pathways:end -->
